Solve the following equation, algebraically, over the interval \([0,2 \pi]\).
\[
5 \cos ^{2} \theta-\cos \theta-\sin ^{2} \theta=0
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{array}{ll}
5 \cos ^{2} \theta-\cos \theta-\left(1-\cos ^{2} \theta\right) & =0 \\
5 \cos ^{2} \theta-\cos \theta-1+\cos ^{2} \theta & =0 \\
6 \cos ^{2} \theta-\cos \theta-1 & =0 \\
(3 \cos \theta+1)(2 \cos \theta-1) & =0 \\
\cos \theta=-\frac{1}{3} \quad \cos \theta=\frac{1}{2} \quad & 1 \text { mark for substitution of an appropriate identity } \\
\theta_{r}=1.230959 \quad & 1 \text { mark for solving for } \cos \theta\left(\frac{1}{2} \text { mark for each branch }\right) \\
\theta=1.911,4.373 \quad \theta=\frac{\pi}{3}, \frac{5 \pi}{3} \quad 2 \text { marks for solving for } \theta\left(\frac{1}{2} \text { mark for each value of } \theta\right) \\
\theta=1.911,4.373 \quad \text { or } \quad \theta=1.047,5.236 \quad \text { 4 marks }
\end{array}
\]

